From 39dda0fb184c7cdd0bbe89ea9bf314f036606da3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:45:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Accept date-stamped split-period uploads and merge them month
 by month

- Filenames: '<YYYY> Sales Analysis by customer <ddmmyyyy>.xlsx' (and the other
  year-bearing exports) now accept an optional trailing date stamp.
- Uploading a new date-stamped invoice file no longer soft-deletes every other
  file for the year; only a same-name re-upload is superseded.
- Customer sync, the weekly board and the HQ report take each calendar month
  from the newest file with data in that month (lib/periods.js), so period-only
  files add up and YTD re-exports still replace older copies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
